tinymsis adapts the NRLMSISE-00 model by Mike Picone, Alan Hedin, and Doug Drob
(Naval Research Laboratory), and the C implementation by Dominik Brodowski.
Original C source: https://git.linta.de/~brodo/nrlmsise-00.git/
Commit: bc9a2feba4344e74201281e563332688a4d09cc3 (2019-07-09).
The original C/data authorship comments are retained in adapted source files.

TinyNadir changes: caller-owned context replaces mutable globals; coefficient
arrays const; coefficient clipping is local rather than a table mutation;
spline allocation replaced with bounded stack scratch; diagnostic I/O removed;
private symbol prefixes and an SI, validated-input wrapper. Pressure-to-altitude
inversion is excluded from the selected altitude-input profile.
TinyNadir's new wrapper/adaptations are MIT licensed (LICENSE).

